00:43:59.000 --> 00:44:16.000
Whitney Hodges: between Google and Meta. It can have a compounding effect in terms of you know, when the when tracking is is set up the right way, and in thinking about the the journey of today's buyers, and how they're really all over the place like they're researching.

00:44:16.000 --> 00:44:32.000
Whitney Hodges: everywhere, right? So, yes, they may find you on Google and like what they see, but they might not be ready to inquire just then, right? If Meta ads are running, well, the next time they open up their Instagram or their Facebook, if they're on Facebook.

00:44:26.000 --> 00:44:27.000
The Organic Moment Photo + Video: Mmhm.

00:44:32.000 --> 00:44:48.000
Whitney Hodges: it can be set up based on pixel data that's, you know, tracking on the website to where they're then seeing ads from you on those platforms, right? It's like they're getting a reminder, they're getting more of that visibility, brand awareness from you, um, or even.

00:44:48.000 --> 00:45:03.000
Whitney Hodges: um, what we would call, like, direct response ads, something that's telling them specifically to take the next step, and here's how we're going to guide you through it, sort of thing. Um, so that typically is our strategy, is our recommendation, right? Like.

00:44:59.000 --> 00:45:00.000
The Organic Moment Photo + Video: Mm-hmm.

00:45:03.000 --> 00:45:22.000
Whitney Hodges: if you have the funds available, instead of just putting it all in Google, or putting it all in Meta, splitting it, um, between both. Um, and the photographers that we work with, elopement photographers included, um, we're oftentimes seeing a better cost per lead.

00:45:22.000 --> 00:45:41.000
Whitney Hodges: from leads that are coming in on the Meta ad side than on the Google ads side. So we do really see them working together and working in tandem. That's not to say that you have to start with Meta, like, straight out of the gate. It's always something that could be.

00:45:41.000 --> 00:45:54.000
Whitney Hodges: layered on later. Another really important piece of the strategy that I want you to kind of keep in mind and kind of be thinking about in terms of like the timeline of when you would want to dive into this.

00:45:54.000 --> 00:46:01.000
Whitney Hodges: is that with Google Ads, you absolutely can just send that traffic to your website.

00:46:01.000 --> 00:46:21.000
Whitney Hodges: But what we find is typically most effective is sending that traffic to a dedicated, long-form landing page. So, it can be a part of your website, but it's more of, like, a hidden page of your website to where they can't navigate to other tabs, they can't go anywhere else, there's just one clear next step for them, which would be.

00:46:21.000 --> 00:46:30.000
Whitney Hodges: to inquire with you. So, I'm curious if that was also a recommendation of the Google Ads team that you worked with, and that was… if that was kind of what you were doing.

00:46:28.000 --> 00:46:30.000
The Organic Moment Photo + Video: It is what we do.

